 ## 4. Design system

-4.1. **shadcn's tokens** ([ADR-0103](../adr/0103-shadcn-stock-design.md)). The interface uses shadcn/ui's semantic variables (`background`, `foreground`, `primary`, `muted`, `accent`, `border`, `ring`, `sidebar-*`, `chart-*`) from its `mist` base colour with the `indigo` theme, generated by `@plux/brand` into `theme.gen.css`; `styles/surfaces.css` adds the colour wash, elevation and frosted glass on shadcn's `data-slot`s. Studio adds only what shadcn has no token for (status, selection and arrow colours, the sample-app colours); older Studio token names remain as aliases of shadcn's variables until no screen uses them. Brand tokens (Appendix J) feed the wordmark and Plux Canvas.
+4.1. **shadcn's tokens** ([ADR-0103](../adr/0103-shadcn-stock-design.md)). The interface uses shadcn/ui's semantic variables (`background`, `foreground`, `primary`, `muted`, `accent`, `border`, `ring`, `sidebar-*`, `chart-*`) from its `zinc` base colour with the `indigo` theme, generated by `@plux/brand` into `theme.gen.css`; `styles/surfaces.css` sets the shell's planes apart and adds elevation and frosted glass (the `.glass` surface) on shadcn's `data-slot`s. Colour comes in small solid marks, never washes or glows. Studio adds only what shadcn has no token for (status, selection and arrow colours, the sample-app colours); older Studio token names remain as aliases of shadcn's variables until no screen uses them. Brand tokens (Appendix J) feed the wordmark and Plux Canvas.

 4.2. **No raw values in Studio's code.** No hex, `rgb()`, `hsl()`, pixel, `rem` or shadow literals in Studio's components, and no Tailwind arbitrary values (`bg-[#…]`, `p-[13px]`, `rounded-[…]`); Tailwind's default scale and shadcn's semantic utilities are used instead. A lint rule enforces this. shadcn's own components in `studio/packages/ui/src/components/` are exempt: they are kept as shadcn ships them (ADR-0103). No runtime CSS-in-JS.

-4.3. **The visual language is shadcn/ui as it ships** ([ADR-0103](../adr/0103-shadcn-stock-design.md), maintainer, 2026-10-30): Base UI, the `nova` style, the `mist` base colour with the `indigo` theme (amended 2026-10-31), Inter and lucide; shadcn's layouts and blocks for whole screens (the sidebar layout for the signed-in shell, `login-02` for sign-in, section cards, items, empty states). A screen is composed from shadcn's components and blocks before anything is written by hand; the official shadcn agent skill (`.claude/skills/shadcn`) holds the composition rules. The Porcelain sections of [studio-ui-language.md](studio-ui-language.md) no longer describe the interface.
+4.3. **The visual language is shadcn/ui as it ships** ([ADR-0103](../adr/0103-shadcn-stock-design.md), maintainer, 2026-10-30): Base UI, the `nova` style, the `zinc` base colour with the `indigo` theme (amended 2026-11-01), Inter and lucide; shadcn's layouts and blocks for whole screens (the sidebar layout for the signed-in shell, `login-02` for sign-in, section cards, items, empty states). A screen is composed from shadcn's components and blocks before anything is written by hand; the official shadcn agent skill (`.claude/skills/shadcn`) holds the composition rules. The Porcelain sections of [studio-ui-language.md](studio-ui-language.md) no longer describe the interface.

 4.4. **Themes and density** (`STU-014`): light, dark and system; compact density by default and comfortable as the option, both as token sets (CSS variables), not conditional class names. A high-contrast theme exists for the canvas preview (`STU-112`) and is offered for the shell.

